cowiconman(1) "@VERSION@" "cowiconman - cow window icon manager"

# NAME

cowiconman - CoW Icon Manager

# SYNOPSIS

*cowiconman* [*--output* _NAME_|*@N*|*current*|*self*]++
[*--desk* _N_|*current*] [*--page* _X,Y_|*current*]++
[*--sort* *none*|*title*|*app*|*id*]++
[*--group-by* *none*|*app*|*title*|*output*|*desk*]++
[*--match* _FIELD_=_TEXT_]++
[*--format* _FMT_]++
[*--rows* _N_] [*--cols* _N_] [*--anchor* *none*|*top*|*bottom*]++
[*--button-width* _N_] [*--button-height* _N_]++
[*--min-button-width* _N_]++
[*--icons*] [*--icon-size* _N_]++
[*--iconified-marker*] [*--show-self*]

# DESCRIPTION

*cowiconman* displays a clickable list of windows known to *cow*(1).  

With no filters, all windows are shown.  Filters combine, so an output, desk,
and page filter together show only windows matching all three.

The window size follows the visible button grid, growing or shrinking as
windows enter or leave the list.  It is capped to the selected output's usable
area.

# APPEARANCE

Focused and unfocused rows use the active and inactive titlebar colours.

# OPTIONS

*--output* _VALUE_
	Limit the list to an output.  _VALUE_ may be an output name, *@N* for
	cow's output number, *current* for cow's current output, or *self* for
	the output containing the cowiconman window.

*--desk* _VALUE_
	Limit the list to a desk.  _VALUE_ may be a desk number or *current*.

*--page* _VALUE_
	Limit the list to a page.  _VALUE_ may be _X,Y_ or *current*.

*--sort* _MODE_
	Sort rows by *title*, *app*, *id*, or leave them in cow's order with
	*none*.  The default is *title*.

*--group-by* _MODE_
	Group matching windows into one row.  _MODE_ may be *none*, *app*,
	*title*, *output*, or *desk*.  The default is *none*.

*--match* _FIELD_=_TEXT_
	Only show windows whose _FIELD_ contains _TEXT_.  _FIELD_ may be
	*title*, *app*, or *id*.  Matching is case-insensitive and the option
	may be repeated.  Prefix _TEXT_ with *!* to exclude matching windows.

*--format* _FMT_
	Row label format.  Supported escapes are *%t* title, *%a* app_id,
	*%i* short window id, *%o* output, *%d* desk, and *%%*.

*--rows* _N_
	Arrange buttons into at most _N_ rows before starting a new column.

*--cols* _N_
	Arrange buttons into _N_ columns.  The number of rows is computed from
	the visible window count.

*--anchor* _VALUE_
	Move the cowiconman window to the selected output's *top* or *bottom*
	usable edge.  The default is *none*.

*--button-width* _N_
	Preferred button width in pixels.  The default is 300.

*--button-height* _N_
	Override the row height derived from cow's current titlebar theme.

*--min-button-width* _N_
	Minimum button width used when the preferred grid would exceed the
	output's usable width.  The default is 80.

*--icons*
	Show each window's application icon before its label.  cowiconman uses
	the icon resolved by cow.

*--icon-size* _N_
	Set the application icon size in pixels.  The default is 16 and the
	maximum is 20.

*--iconified-marker*
	Reserve space before each label and draw a small square there for
	iconified windows.

*--show-self*
	Include cowiconman windows in the list.  They are hidden by default.

*-h*, *--help*
	Print usage and exit.

# USAGE

Left-click a row to focus the window.  If the window is iconified, it is
restored and focused.

Left-click a grouped row to open a selector for the windows in that group.
The selector is a native cow menu using the current menu style.  Its rows
include the short window id, output, and desk.  Selecting a window switches to
its output, desk, and page, activates its container member when necessary,
restores it when iconified, and focuses it.  Type-ahead is disabled for these
selectors; number keys, arrows, Enter, and Escape remain available.

Middle-click a row to toggle the window's iconified state.

Use the pointer wheel to scroll when a fixed row layout has more entries than
fit on screen.

An anchored *--rows 1* layout behaves like a bar: it spans the selected
output's usable width and divides that space evenly between entries.

# EXAMPLES

Show every window:

```
cowiconman &
```

Show only windows on the current desk and page:

```
cowiconman --desk current --page current &
```

Run a manager for a specific output:

```
cowiconman --output DP-1 &
```

Use cow's output number and preserve cow's window order:

```
cowiconman --output @2 --sort none &
```

Use a two-column layout:

```
cowiconman --cols 2 &
```

Group windows by application:

```
cowiconman --group-by app &
```

Show only xterm windows:

```
cowiconman --match app=xterm &
```

Hide xterm windows:

```
cowiconman --match app=!xterm &
```

Use a one-row top task list for the current output:

```
cowiconman --output current --rows 1 --anchor top &
```

Show an iconified-window marker before labels:

```
cowiconman --iconified-marker &
```

Show 16-pixel application icons before labels:

```
cowiconman --icons &
```

Remove the border, handles, and titlebar from cowiconman while preserving
the active decor theme:

```
decor -d cowiconman-chrome border.width 0
decor -d cowiconman-chrome border.handles false
decor -d cowiconman-chrome titlebar.enabled false
rule -g -Ton-map -ncowiconman-chrome -s %cowiconman decor -a cowiconman-chrome
```

# SEE ALSO

*cow*(1), *moocow*(1), *cowpager*(1)

